fails, raise before permitting worktree reuse. Keep valid duplicate snapshots reusable.","id":"863b1d72838c548dd694444d639bb457f36b027973bf9d22b93e5010fe1e4dc9","intervals":[[105,105]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/retain.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Verify an existing snapshot before returning success."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"241afa9b4e62e325ab2d3b27e1c4b2c35d1be60c","body":"**Handle `TimeoutExpired` in the cleanup path.**\n\n`command()` sets a 1200-second default timeout. When the timeout expires, it kills the process group and re-raises `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`. `cleanup_harvested()` calls `command()` for the status check at line 36, so the exception propagates out of cleanup. `TimeoutExpired` derives from `SubprocessError`, not from the exception types caught at `repair_tick.py:457`. The timeout therefore skips the `messages.append` recording and exits the `harvest()` loop. Remaining verdicts and items for that tick are not processed.\n\nCatch `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` at the cleanup call site, or add it to the handler's exception tuple. Record the failure and continue. The status check runs before worktree removal, so the worktree stays available for a later attempt.","id":"3ca070bae3a00cc91f6e0b84872b47ce014eedfb3fdec40d1baa00350fdf1ef9","intervals":[[36,36]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/retain.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Handle `TimeoutExpired` in the cleanup path."}],"head":"47640a4b55bb06ebfa85496e3ae2aebe1906b6bc","head_tree":"0d65d4810f33ebd3f59ceadb6cd04b9dbafa38fc","input_scope":[{"blob":"241afa9b4e62e325ab2d3b27e1c4b2c35d1be60c","intervals":[[1,119]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/retain.py"}],"job_id":"fb03dc99823af10e4bc6a56c218506d2955bb9af624c78f60164d10d5efbaf06:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"241afa9b4e62e325ab2d3b27e1c4b2c35d1be60c","disposition":"included","mod